  "slug": "cell-cell-analysis-ceea",
  "summary": "Reanalysis of public single-cell and bulk cohorts is now producing candidate prognostic and functional markers across several tumor types.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reanalysis of public and multi-omic cohorts to resolve tumor cell states and attach candidate biomarkers to them. Several studies pair scRNA-seq with bulk data. Osteosarcoma reanalysis (GSE162454) identifies a recurrent proliferative/mitotic malignant state, and TROAP knockdown reduces colony formation. Thyroid scRNA-seq of 17 PTC samples reveals a CRABP1-positive state linked to metastasis, with methylation-associated downregulation. FAM72D in HCC associates with a FOXM1-driven proliferative state. Others extend this logic to spatial and pan-cancer resources: CosMx mapping of 11 ADC targets across 154,816 breast tumor cells, and a TCGA-based glycoRNA-related program score across 9,186 tumors. The HPV integration, skin adnexal genomics, and radiotherapy response studies address distinct questions and are not part of this thread. Functional knockdown testing of candidate genes recurs across several studies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-14"
}
